==German==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|de|gmh|vinster}}, from {{inh|de|goh|finstar}}, from {{inh|de|gem-pro|*finistraz}}, alteration (with the dental and labial articulations switching their positions) of {{inh|de|gem-pro|*þimistraz}}. From the ''þ''-form also {{cog|goh|thinstar}} ({{cog|gmh|dinster}}), {{cog|odt|*thimister}} ({{cog|nl|deemster}}); from the ''f''-form {{cog|odt|finistre}}, {{cog|osx|finistar}}. Related with {{cog|de|dämmern}}. Perhaps also related with {{m+|gem-pro|*þiustrijaz}}, whence {{m+|de|düster}}, {{m|de|duster}}.

